---
title: The life of a problem entry
---
flowchart TD
    classDef human fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#8a6d3b,color:#000
    classDef role fill:#d9edf7,stroke:#31708f,color:#000
    classDef channel fill:#dff0d8,stroke:#3c763d,color:#000
    classDef gate fill:#f2dede,stroke:#a94442,color:#000
    classDef stop fill:#eeeeee,stroke:#777,color:#000

    SRC1["Coder — something real,<br/>outside the current subtask's scope"]:::role
    SRC2["Human — a defect found reviewing<br/>one finished subtask"]:::human
    SRC3["Milestone Reviewer — what per-subtask<br/>review structurally could not see"]:::role
    SRC4["Architect — a judgement call, a design<br/>question, a finding from a project review,<br/>with its evidence in the entry"]:::role

    PROB[".claude/problems.md — the open queue:<br/>P-n title, Created by: role,<br/>Importance: and Effort: from the filer,<br/>Thinking: and Decision: from the Architect,<br/>Reason, Description,<br/>How to prevent in future.<br/>Number taken from the 'Next entry:' line"]:::channel

    NEXT(["Human asks for the next task"]):::human
    TW["Task writer reads problems.md<br/>before docs/ROADMAP.md"]:::role
    WHO{"Thinking: 1–4<br/>and Decision: Will do?"}
    WHOSE{"Whose files does the fix touch?"}

    SKIP["Thinking 5–10, or not yet rated:<br/>left in the queue, not deleted.<br/>Listed in the reply so the human<br/>knows what is waiting on a decision"]:::stop
    ARCHFIX["Architect-owned files — an ADR,<br/>CLAUDE.md, README.md, roadmap prose,<br/>a diagram, a role definition.<br/>The Architect fixes it and deletes the<br/>entry, whoever signed it, and says<br/>in its reply which it consumed.<br/>A mixed entry is split, and stays<br/>until both halves are done"]:::role
    HUMANCALL{"Human decides"}:::human
    ARCHINV["Architect takes it back<br/>— see agent-flow-investigation.mmd"]:::role
    ARCHTASK["Architect writes .claude/task.md itself,<br/>bound by task-writer.md, and deletes<br/>the entry in the same edit"]
    DELINV["Settled instead: the conclusion graduates<br/>to an ADR, a roadmap entry or CLAUDE.md,<br/>and only then is the entry deleted"]:::stop

    REVIEW(["Human asks for a triage —<br/>a task, a sub-milestone or a<br/>milestone has just finished"]):::human
    ARCHREV["Architect adds Thinking: and Decision:<br/>to every entry, whoever signed it, and<br/>corrects an Importance: or Effort:<br/>the filer got wrong.<br/>Nothing moved, nothing deleted.<br/>Reports the table and stops"]:::role
    APPROVE{"Human reviews the estimates,<br/>edits any by hand, approves"}:::human
    ACCEPT["Backlog: moved to docs/backlog.md<br/>— heading, one or two sentences,<br/>Created: date, Importance:, Effort:,<br/>Thinking:, each on its own line,<br/>entries split by ---<br/>— and deleted from problems.md in<br/>the same edit. The one deletion that<br/>crosses the signature.<br/>Nobody schedules from that file"]:::stop
    REVIVE{"Architect proposes a revive:<br/>says which entry and what changed,<br/>then stops. The human decides"}:::human
    REVIVED["Approved: the Architect deletes the<br/>backlog entry and files a fresh P- entry<br/>citing it, in the same edit. A problem<br/>whose code is gone is deleted outright<br/>instead, and nothing re-enters the queue"]:::role
    WILLDO["Will do: stays in the queue with all<br/>four fields, which the Task writer<br/>orders the subtasks by"]:::channel

    ANYOPEN{"Anything schedulable left?"}
    MILESTONE(["Next milestone instead<br/>— see agent-flow-milestone-planning.mmd"]):::stop

    TASK["Write .claude/task.md: one subtask per<br/>problem, heading keeping the P-n,<br/>the entry's SP on the Order Plan line,<br/>restating everything the fix needs<br/>including the prevention"]
    CONSUME["Delete the entry from problems.md<br/>in the same edit. It has moved, not gone:<br/>the subtask is where it lives now.<br/>No roadmap status changes — repair<br/>is not milestone progress"]

    CODER(["Coder works one subtask<br/>— see agent-flow-task-implementation.mmd"]):::role
    GATE["Gate green. Set the subtask 👀 Review<br/>in task.md; the human sets ✅ Done.<br/>Nothing to close in problems.md —<br/>the entry is already gone"]:::gate
    CR(["Human checks the fix<br/>and its prevention, then commits"]):::human
    RECORD["The commit is the only lasting record<br/>of what was found. task.md is not archived:<br/>the human empties it once the whole<br/>task has been accepted"]:::stop

    SRC1 --> PROB
    SRC2 --> PROB
    SRC3 --> PROB
    SRC4 --> PROB

    PROB --> REVIEW --> ARCHREV --> APPROVE
    APPROVE -- "Decision: Backlog" --> ACCEPT
    APPROVE -- "Decision: Will do" --> WILLDO --> PROB
    ACCEPT -.-> REVIVE
    REVIVE -- "human approves" --> REVIVED --> PROB

    NEXT --> TW --> WHO
    WHO -- "no — 5–10 is a question,<br/>not a job; never scheduled,<br/>even if the human names it" --> SKIP --> HUMANCALL
    HUMANCALL -- "hands it to the Architect —<br/>the one route a 5–10 entry has" --> ARCHINV
    ARCHINV -- "decided: it needs code" --> ARCHTASK --> CODER
    ARCHINV -- "decided: no code needed" --> DELINV
    ARCHINV -- "decided: minor and expensive —<br/>put it up for the next triage" --> ARCHREV
    WHO -- "yes — 1–4 and decided,<br/>whoever signed it" --> WHOSE
    WHOSE -- "Architect's" --> ARCHFIX
    WHOSE -- "Coder's" --> ANYOPEN
    ANYOPEN -- no --> MILESTONE
    ANYOPEN -- yes --> TASK --> CONSUME --> CODER --> GATE --> CR --> RECORD
